    "https://www.jobs.gla.ac.uk/job/barista-6013276?source=google.com": {
      "title": "Barista",
      "description": "Barista · University of Glasgow This website uses cookies to ensure you get the best experience. read more Got it! Vacancies About Us Contact Why UofG Login Register Login Menu Vacancies About Us Why UofG Contact Sign In Home Jobs Barista Barista Back to jobs Barista Job details Posted 01 September 2026 Salary £13.45 per hour Location Glasgow Job Type Operational Reference 207034 Expiry 15 Sep 2026 23:45 Job description Job Purpose As a Barista, for a well-known Glasgow brand, you will cover all elements of the operation, both front of house customer service and presentation and delivery of the food offering. We are looking for a skilled barista to contribute to deliver an atmosphere where guests have a great customer experience, that is both welcoming and engaging. We are a fast-paced team who pride ourselves in making great coffee. You will be a key team player and demonstrate passion and pride in what you do. Main Duties and Responsibilities 1. To assist in the preparation and provision of all food and drinks being served and to ensure that this meets the required standards of the Food Safety Policy. 2. Ensure thorough and up to date knowledge and understanding of menu and special offers, in order to provide relevant information to our customers. 3. To ensure the hygiene, cleanliness and tidiness of the catering and café areas, whilst adhering to Health and Safety and Hygiene policies. 4. Demonstrate a passion for customer service excellence and offer a personalised service experience that exceeds customer expectation. 5. Responsible for cash handling in line with cash handling procedures. 6. Liaise and communicate with customers and colleagues to ensure the smooth and efficient running of the department. 7. To assist in the control of food and non-food items ensuring that the compliance of the department policies on storage and issuing of all stock procedures are always adhered to. This will include assisting with stocktaking. 8. Demonstrate a positive attitude and flexible working approach to meet the demands of the operation or individual units. 9. Meet all legislative and policy requirements including COSHH. Knowledge, Qualifications, Skills and Experience Knowledge/Qualifications Essential: A1 Ability to demonstrate the competencies to undertake the duties associated with this level of post having acquired the necessary knowledge and skills in a similar role. A2 Food Safety Level 1 (to be completed within first week) followed by Food Safety Level 2 (to be completed within first 3 months). A3 Good working knowledge of Food Safety and Health and Safety Awareness. Desirable: B1 Food Safety Level 2. B2 Allergen Awareness. Skills Essential: C1 Ability to work well under pressure. C2 Basic computer skills and experience. C3 Excellent communication and interpersonal skills. C4 Adaptable and Flexible approach to work. C5 Strong organisational and customer service skills. C6 Team player who is committed and enthusiastic. C7 Strong understanding of coffee and latte art. Experience Essential: E1 Demonstrable previous experience of working in a customer facing environment. E2 Experience of working independently and as part of a team. E3 Previous experience of operating a till system. Terms & Conditions For a well-known Glasgow brand. Salary will be £13.45 per hour. This post is open ended and part time (fractional) for a minimum 10 hours per month. Closing date: 15 September 2026 UoG Commercial Ltd is a subsidiary company wholly owned by the University of Glasgow and provides catering services as part of the new extended campus at the University. As our employees are integrally involved in generating and sharing in the business' success, including a share of the profits. We want our customers and partners to feel equally valued and appreciated because they are both important to our success. We recognise that the way we conduct ourselves reflects not just on the company, but the University of Glasgow and so our values are at the heart of the way in which we behave. Put simply we ask our employees to: Be friendly and positive Treat everyone with respect Take pride in everything they do What we can offer you *           Subsidised meals on duty *           Fantastic opportunities for career growth and development *           Brilliant culture, where we have fun and work hard *           Great work life balance *           Access to UoG benefit scheme *           Discounted sport membership at UoG Sport If this sounds like the right role for you, we'd love to hear from you! Apply Now Save this job Barista Glasgow Posted 2 days ago Apply Now Share this job linkedin twitter facebook mail whatsapp Sign up for job alerts Sign in or register here to receive emails about new jobs like these You agree to our Terms & conditions Latest Jobs Organisational Development Partner Glasgow Grade 8, £50,253 - £58,225 per annum Barista Glasgow £13.45 per hour Support Administrator Glasgow Grade 3, £24,685 - £25,249 per annum Clinician in Anaesthesia Glasgow Grade 7/8: £41,064 - £46,049/£50,253 - £58,225 per annum pro rata Student Ambassador Glasgow £24,685 pa -  £25,804 pa logo The University of Glasgow is a registered Scottishcharity: Registration Number SC004401 X Facebook instagram Legal Cookies Terms of use PeopleXD accessibilty statement Candidate privacy notice Accreditation Quick Links About Contact Us Vacancies Salaries Applicant Guide All Right Reserved 2026 University of Glasgow Recruitment website by"
