    "https://www.jobs.gla.ac.uk/job/support-administrator-6011573?source=google.com": {
      "title": "Support Administrator",
      "description": "Support Administrator · University of Glasgow This website uses cookies to ensure you get the best experience. read more Got it! Vacancies About Us Contact Why UofG Login Register Login Menu Vacancies About Us Why UofG Contact Sign In Home Jobs Support Administrator Support Administrator Back to jobs Support Administrator Job details Posted 28 August 2026 Salary Grade 3, £24,685 - £25,249 per annum Location Glasgow Job Type Management Professional & Administrative Reference 203833 Expiry 11 Sep 2026 23:45 Job description Job Purpose The Support Administrator role will assist the Academic and Digital Development Adviser with planning and co-ordinating their diary, monitoring and supporting communications and collating actions from monitored communications. The postholder will provide ongoing, specific and assistive support to the Academic and Digital Development Adviser, who has a disability, to enable them to undertake the key preparation and diary management administrative activities of this Adviser role. The Support Administrator will also assist with processing and submission of Access to Work claims. Main Duties and Responsibilities Assist the Academic and Digital Development Adviser, as part of the Academic and Digital Development (ADD) team, in planning and prioritising work activities and support the Adviser with responding to conflicting demands. This will involve reviewing emails, suggesting action points, attending approximately weekly meetings, occasionally liaising with the Advisor’s line manager and collaboratively reviewing their current and upcoming workload, workstreams, and obligations. Set short term priorities or work schedules, assigning straightforward and routine tasks to   others, to ensure operational efficiency. Collaborate and advise on the administrative and organisational aspects of the Academic and Digital Development Adviser’s workload. This will include diary and time management, setting reminders to optimise workflow and utilising knowledge of the appropriate departments and service relevant to ADD operations. Resolve administrative issues, e.g, diary conflicts, applying sound judgement based on experience, largely without reference to others to provide an effective service and clear advice to colleagues and customers. Deliver a range of administrative and/or customer service activities to maximise service quality and continuity including sending follow-up communications email on behalf of the Academic and Digital Development Adviser or preparing straightforward analysis, manipulation and interpretation of data. May include limited supervisory responsibility. Some tasks will require the same skills and responsibilities as limited supervision. For example, monitoring task progress and advising on organisation and workload. Knowledge, Qualifications, Skills and Experience Knowledge/Qualifications Essential: A1 Ability to demonstrate the competencies required to undertake the duties associated with this level of post having acquired the necessary knowledge and skills in a similar role. A2 Detailed knowledge of relevant systems such as Microsoft Office and Outlook, equipment, processes and procedures including software packages. A3 Understanding of relevant policies and procedures relative to the role, and the quality standards and outputs required. Desirable: B1 Knowledge of ADD services and procedures relevant to ADD operations. Skills Essential: C1 Effective planning, organising and prioritising. C2 Ability to plan or schedule work days and weeks ahead, and to respond to changing pressures or requirements. C3 Good level of IT competence including familiarity Microsoft Office, and Outlook. C4 Ability to undertake assigned tasks in a timely manner and to an acceptable standard C5 Initiative and judgement to resolve problems independently. C6 Excellent interpersonal skills with the ability to communicate clearly, clarifying requirements, responding to colleagues and customers. C7 Good attention to detail. Experience Essential: E1 Experience of diary coordination and diary management using Outlook. E2 Experience of providing administration support using Microsoft Office. Desirable: F1 Experience working with neurodiverse colleagues. Terms and Conditions Salary will be Grade 3, £24,685 - £25,249 per annum pro rata. This post is part-time (up to 7 hours per week, working hours will be agreed with the successful candidate), and open ended with funding available for up to the 15th March 2029 in the first instance. Closing date: 23:45 11th September 2026 As a valued member of our team, you can expect: 1 A warm welcoming and engaging organisational culture, where your talents are developed and nurtured, and success is celebrated and shared. 2 An excellent employment package with generous terms and conditions including 41 days of leave for full time staff, pension - pensions handbook https://www.gla.ac.uk/myglasgow/payandpensions/pensions/, benefits and discount packages. 3 A flexible approach to working. 4 A commitment to support your health and wellbeing, including a free 6-month UofG Sport membership for all new staff joining the University  https://www.gla.ac.uk/myglasgow/staff/healthwellbeing/. We believe that we can only reach our full potential through the talents of all. Equality, diversity and inclusion are at the heart of our values. Applications are particularly welcome from across our communities and in particular people from the Black, Asian and Minority Ethnic (BAME) community, and other protected characteristics who are under-represented within the University. Read more on how the University promotes and embeds all aspects of equality and diversity within our community https://www.gla.ac.uk/myglasgow/humanresources/equalitydiversity/. We endorse the principles of Athena Swan https://www.gla.ac.uk/myglasgow/humanresources/equalitydiversity/athenaswan/ and hold bronze, silver and gold awards across the University. We are investing in our organisation, and we will invest in you too. Please visit our website https://www.gla.ac.uk/explore/jobs/ for more information. Apply Now Save this job Support Administrator Glasgow Posted 6 days ago Apply Now Share this job linkedin twitter facebook mail whatsapp Sign up for job alerts Sign in or register here to receive emails about new jobs like these You agree to our Terms & conditions Latest Jobs Organisational Development Partner Glasgow Grade 8, £50,253 - £58,225 per annum Barista Glasgow £13.45 per hour Support Administrator Glasgow Grade 3, £24,685 - £25,249 per annum Clinician in Anaesthesia Glasgow Grade 7/8: £41,064 - £46,049/£50,253 - £58,225 per annum pro rata Student Ambassador Glasgow £24,685 pa -  £25,804 pa logo The University of Glasgow is a registered Scottishcharity: Registration Number SC004401 X Facebook instagram Legal Cookies Terms of use PeopleXD accessibilty statement Candidate privacy notice Accreditation Quick Links About Contact Us Vacancies Salaries Applicant Guide All Right Reserved 2026 University of Glasgow Recruitment website by"
