    "https://www.jobs.gla.ac.uk/job/assistant-demonstrator-school-of-computing-science-6007597?source=google.com": {
      "title": "Assistant Demonstrator",
      "description": "Assistant Demonstrator - School of Computing · University of Glasgow This website uses cookies to ensure you get the best experience. read more Got it! Vacancies About Us Contact Why UofG Login Register Login Menu Vacancies About Us Why UofG Contact Sign In Home Jobs Assistant Demonstrator - School of Computing Science Assistant Demonstrator - School of Computing Science Back to jobs Assistant Demonstrator - School of Computing Science Job details Posted 27 August 2026 Location Glasgow Job Type GTA and Demonstrator Reference 206453 Expiry 05 Feb 2027 22:45 Job description Applications for this post will only be processed where you are a University of Glasgow student and have been given the vacancy number by your Local School Administrator Job Purpose To provide assistance and laboratory support to academic and student service users. Work will support the smooth and effective running of teaching laboratories in line with the College/Institute/School Strategy. Main Duties and Responsibilities 1.        Provide knowledge exchange support to academic and student service users within the specified discipline. Contribute to the overall smooth and efficient running of the lab to ensure an excellent experience for service users. 2.        Carry out a range of technical support activities including the use of specialist equipment, systems, procedures, protocols, models and/or techniques. Contribute to the creation and development of new technical resources and/or ways of working as directed by relevant senior staff. Identify, propose and implement technical solutions to a range of practical problems. 3.        Keep clear and accurate records of teaching outputs and where relevant produce concise written summaries of results for senior staff. 4.        Contribute to the well-organised functioning of the laboratory. Maintain laboratory areas appropriately and identify and seek support to rectify any technical faults/problems with equipment. 5.        To provide guidance to service users in the best application and operation of technical resources. 6.        Keep up to date with advances in the relevant discipline and seek to apply this knowledge to technical activities to further enhance the learning experience and/or contribute to the delivery of research aims. Qualifications *          Scottish Credit and Qualification Framework level 5 or 6 [National 5 or 6, Scottish Vocational Qualification level 2 or 3] or equivalent, and experience of personal development in a similar role. *          Detailed technical knowledge of relevant systems, equipment, protocols, processes and procedures. Knowledge, Skills and Experience *          Demonstrable technical skills aligned to the specified discipline. Details of the discipline are as described in the post-specific information and advert. *          Strong IT skills including both standard and specialist software programmes. *          Ability to work effectively with others, including own team and lab users. *          Ability to plan and prioritise workload to meet competing demands. *          Ability to work independently, including the ability to use initiative and judgement to resolve problems. *          Accuracy and attention to detail. *          Demonstrable work experience in a similar technical role, with similar responsibilities. *          Experience of contributing to the creation or development of technical resources or ways of working. *          Experience of planning and organising own workload to meet the needs of service users. Apply Now Save this job Assistant Demonstrator - School of Computing Science Glasgow Posted 8 days ago Apply Now Share this job linkedin twitter facebook mail whatsapp Sign up for job alerts Sign in or register here to receive emails about new jobs like these You agree to our Terms & conditions Latest Jobs Organisational Development Partner Glasgow Grade 8, £50,253 - £58,225 per annum Barista Glasgow £13.45 per hour Support Administrator Glasgow Grade 3, £24,685 - £25,249 per annum Clinician in Anaesthesia Glasgow Grade 7/8: £41,064 - £46,049/£50,253 - £58,225 per annum pro rata Student Ambassador Glasgow £24,685 pa -  £25,804 pa logo The University of Glasgow is a registered Scottishcharity: Registration Number SC004401 X Facebook instagram Legal Cookies Terms of use PeopleXD accessibilty statement Candidate privacy notice Accreditation Quick Links About Contact Us Vacancies Salaries Applicant Guide All Right Reserved 2026 University of Glasgow Recruitment website by"
