      "description": "Reach Out Library Student Ambassador · University of Glasgow This website uses cookies to ensure you get the best experience. read more Got it! Vacancies About Us Contact Why UofG Login Register Login Menu Vacancies About Us Why UofG Contact Sign In Home Jobs Reach Out Library Student Ambassador Reach Out Library Student Ambassador Back to jobs Reach Out Library Student Ambassador Job details Posted 14 September 2026 Salary Grade 3, £24,685 – £25,249 per annum Location Glasgow Job Type Management Professional & Administrative Reference 208113 Expiry 20 Sep 2026 23:45 Job description Please note, this role is only open to current registered students of University of Glasgow and who are registered until at least May 2027 Job Purpose To provide first-class customer service to all users of the Reach Out service across the University campus, in person and virtually, as part of the Reach Out Library team. Main Duties and Responsibilities 1. Deliver friendly, customer-focused, proactive support to all users of the service and facilities - be visible, maintain a high profile with customers and staff and personally take action to resolve issues and deliver an excellent customer experience, in person and digitally, using UofG Helpdesk. 2. Follow established processes and standard instructions, working as part of the roving student ambassador team to monitor entry with reference to admission and membership policy. Assist with queue management and support correct use of the library entrance gates. 3. Distribute to the correct locations and re-shelve returned items of main library and High Demand Collection stock, according to subject class and call number, to enable readers to find them. On average, c100,000 books are returned to the library or handled for stock maintenance every year. 4. Participate in the ongoing programme of stock maintenance. Carry out regular shelf-checking to ensure that the stock is in the correct location and alerting the supervisor to any problems. Periodically check the security of the RFID tag on High Demand Collection items 5. Apply knowledge of library systems and procedures to actively support students and staff, using UofG Helpdesk to find information and log support requests, highlighting the opportunities for self-service 24/7. Follow established processes and guidelines to resolve common user issues, referring to senior colleagues as appropriate. 6. Carry a mobile device issued to you on duty for team communication and Reach Out support. Perform regular roving support duties including floor checks and reporting faults. Commitment to Health and Safety and to the Don’t Walk By approach. 7. Undertake regular statistics and data collection relating to library services and infrastructure. Participate in ethnographic survey work and user experience data gathering as required. 8. Be an ambassador for the Reach Out ethos, brand and service design principles across all Reach Out locations by: Wearing a Reach Out lanyard and clothing (Tshirt/Sweatshirt) visibly at all times while on duty. Participating in promotion and marketing of Reach Out. Participating in library orientation tours and supporting University Open Days and Welcome events. 9. Following training, assist with building evacuation procedures by providing fire warden support to the Facilities Support team. 10. Any other similar Reach Out duties, as directed by senior colleagues. Knowledge, Qualifications, Skills and Experience Knowledge/Qualifications Essential: A1 Ability to demonstrate the competencies required to undertake the duties associated with this level of post gained through working in a similar role or Scottish Credit and Qualification Framework level 4 in English (National 4) or equivalent, and experience of working in a similar role. Skills Essential: C1 Excellent customer service skills. C2 Good communication and interpersonal skills (written & oral). C3 High standard of accuracy and attention to detail. C4 Good IT skills. C5 Ability to respond to changing work priorities. Experience Essential: E1 Previous work experience. E2 Experience of working in a team environment. E3 Experience of engaging with the public. E4 Experience of dealing with customer records in compliance with the General Data Protection Regulation 2018. Desirable: F1 Experience of working in a library. F2 Experience of taking groups on tours. F3 Experience of using social media. Terms and Conditions Salary will be Grade 3, £24,685 - £25,249 per annum pro rata. This post is offered on a fractional basis (minimum 6 hours a week, maximum 9 hours a week- shifts will be 3 hours in duration eg. 2x3 hours, 3x3 hours) and is fixed term till 22 May 2027. Closing date: 23:45 20th September 2026 As a valued member of our team, you can expect: 1 A warm welcoming and engaging organisational culture, where your talents are developed and nurtured, and success is celebrated and shared. 2 An excellent employment package with generous terms and conditions including 41 days of leave for full time staff, pension - pensions handbook https://www.gla.ac.uk/myglasgow/payandpensions/pensions/, benefits and discount packages. 3 A flexible approach to working. 4 A commitment to support your health and wellbeing, including a free 6-month UofG Sport membership for all new staff joining the University  https://www.gla.ac.uk/myglasgow/staff/healthwellbeing/. We believe that we can only reach our full potential through the talents of all. Equality, diversity and inclusion are at the heart of our values. Applications are particularly welcome from across our communities and in particular people from the Black, Asian and Minority Ethnic (BAME) community, and other protected characteristics who are under-represented within the University. Read more on how the University promotes and embeds all aspects of equality and diversity within our community https://www.gla.ac.uk/myglasgow/humanresources/equalitydiversity/. We endorse the principles of Athena Swan https://www.gla.ac.uk/myglasgow/humanresources/equalitydiversity/athenaswan/ and hold bronze, silver and gold awards across the University. We are investing in our organisation, and we will invest in you too. Please visit our website https://www.gla.ac.uk/explore/jobs/ for more information. Apply Now Save this job Reach Out Library Student Ambassador Glasgow Posted about 16 hours ago Apply Now Share this job linkedin twitter facebook mail whatsapp Sign up for job alerts Sign in or register here to receive emails about new jobs like these You agree to our Terms & conditions Latest Jobs Research Associate Glasgow Grade 7 £41,064 - £46,049 per annum Research Scientist - Scottish Marine Animal Stranding Scheme (SMASS) Glasgow Grade 6 £33,951 - £37,694 Grade 7 £41,064 - £46,049 Reach Out Library Student Ambassador Glasgow Grade 3, £24,685 – £25,249 per annum Byres Community Hub Host Glasgow Grade 4, £25,804 - £27,319 per annum Lifelong Learning Tutor - Access Physics Glasgow Grade 6, £33,951 - £37,694 per annum pro rata logo The University of Glasgow is a registered Scottishcharity: Registration Number SC004401 X Facebook instagram Legal Cookies Terms of use PeopleXD accessibilty statement Candidate privacy notice Accreditation Quick Links About Contact Us Vacancies Salaries Applicant Guide All Right Reserved 2026 University of Glasgow Recruitment website by"
